{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Project Launcher\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Project Launcher puts your recent projects, project templates and project folders in one window. You can search everything, check the project details and open it without digging through folders.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Project templates\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Organize your templates into sections without moving any files. You can check the track list before opening one, then open it as a new project or edit the template itself.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Project folders\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Add your project folders and Project Launcher scans them in the background. It remembers the results, so they are ready the next time you open it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Startup\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Project Launcher can open with REAPER and stay hidden when another project is already open.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Shortcuts\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\f1 Enter} opens the selected project.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\f1 Ctrl/Cmd} + {\f1 Enter} opens it in a new tab. If {\f1 Settings} > {\f1 Open projects in} is set to {\f1 New tab}, it opens in the current tab instead.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\f1 Alt/Option} + {\f1 Enter} opens it as a new version.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\f1 Ctrl/Cmd} + {\f1 F} jumps to search.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\f1 Esc} clears the search or closes the window.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Requirements\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 You need {\b ReaImGui 0.10 or newer}. Project Launcher checks this when it starts and tells you if it is missing.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b js_ReaScriptAPI} is optional. It adds modified dates and a folder picker. {\b SWS} is also optional and lets Project Launcher switch off REAPER's own startup prompt.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Credits and license\par}
